 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "건강 표현: have a + 증상 / should / have to",
   "en": "health problems: have a + symptom, should and have to"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "증상은 'I have a + 증상'으로 말합니다 (I have a headache). 의사의 조언은 should + 동사원형, 꼭 해야 하는 일은 have to로 말합니다. 약은 'Take this medicine twice a day.'처럼 명령문으로 지시합니다.",
   "en": "Say a symptom with 'I have a + symptom' (I have a headache). Advice uses should + base verb; things you must do use have to. Instructions for medicine are imperatives: Take this medicine twice a day."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "have a + 증상",
     "I have a headache. I have a fever."
    ],
    [
     "should + 동사",
     "You should see a doctor."
    ],
    [
     "have to + 동사",
     "You have to rest at home."
    ],
    [
     "명령문 / imperative",
     "Take this medicine twice a day."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "증상: have a headache / a cough / a fever.",
    "en": "Symptoms: have a headache / a cough / a fever."
   },
   {
    "ko": "should = 조언, have to = 꼭 해야 함.",
    "en": "should = advice; have to = necessity."
   },
   {
    "ko": "'~ ache'는 a를 씁니다: a stomach ache.",
    "en": "Use a with ache: a stomach ache."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
